cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you implement or describe this profile, please cite it as below."
title: "txAuthAgent — WebAuthn Agent Authorization Application Profile"
abstract: >-
  An application profile on top of the W3C WebAuthn `sign` extension that
  defines hardware-backed, human-consented authorization for autonomous AI
  agent actions. The profile specifies the action payload schema, the canonical
  digest passed as the `tbs`, the ceremony wiring, and the verification rules
  that let any party verify an agent authorization against the signing public
  key published at registration — without the pairwise WebAuthn credential ever
  being used for third-party verification.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Empire Labs Pty Ltd"
    country: AU
version: "0.4"
date-released: "2026-08-04"
license: MIT
